outing modes
Mode	Behavior	Use case
weighted	Scores all models, picks best	Default, everyday
strict	Uses configured primary	Predictable cost
consensus	N models vote in parallel	High-stakes
fastest	Race — first to respond wins	Real-time UX
cascade	Cheap first, escalate on failure	Budget-tight
Exit codes
Code	Meaning
0	Success
1	Generic error
2	Configuration error
3	Budget exceeded
4	No backend available
5	Router timeout
130	Interrupted (Ctrl+C)
Working files
text

~/.config/nexus/
├── config.toml           # User configuration
├── credentials.toml      # API keys (chmod 600, never committed)
└── history.jsonl         # Request log (opt-in)

~/.cache/nexus/
├── models/               # Local model cache
└── embeddings/           # RAG index

What Nexus does not do

    Does not store your prompts without explicit consent

    Does not make undeclared network calls in config.toml

    Does not persist tokens in clear text

    Does not bypass your OS security policies

    Never writes outside ~/.config/nexus/ and ~/.cache/nexus/
